ENTRY            D1099   20260702   20261124   20261124       D153
SUBENT        D1099001   20260702   20261124   20261124       D153
BIB                 14         31
TITLE      Excitation functions of (p,gamma) and (p,n) reactions
            on zinc up to 4 MeV
AUTHOR     (M.S.Uddin, M.M.Hasan, M.Moniruzzaman, M.A.Shariff,
            S.M.Qaim)
INSTITUTE  (3BANSAV,2GERJUL)
REFERENCE  (J,RCA,113,945,2025)
FACILITY   (VDGT,3BANSAV) 3 MV Tandem accelerator
SAMPLE     Natural zinc foils (99.95% purity), thickness 25 um,
            circular discs of 13 mm diameter, were used as target
            material for proton irradiation.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) 60% relative efficiency, 1.9 keV
            resolution at 1332.6 keV of 60Co
METHOD     (ACTIV) Irradiated for 20 min with proton beam energy
            of 4.4+/-0.03 MeV and constant beam current of 170 nA.
MONITOR    (29-CU-0(P,X)30-ZN-65,,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (,A.Hermanne+,J,NDS,148,338,2018)
CORRECTION  Corrected for:
           . gamma-ray intensity
           . detector efficiency
           . coincidence losses
STATUS     (APRVD) Proof-read by M.S.Uddin (2026-07-03)
           (TABLE,,M.S.Uddin+,J,RCA,113,945,2025) Table 1 and 2
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total uncertainty (8-14%) are propagated from:
           (ERR-S,0.1,10.) Counting statistics (0.1-10%)
           (ERR-1) Detector efficiency (4%)
           (ERR-2,0.015,1.3) Half-life of product (0.015-1.3%)
           (ERR-3,0.05,24.) Gamma-ray intensity (0.05-24%)
           (ERR-4,,0.5) Coincidence loss (<0.5%)
           (ERR-5,,1.) Number of target nuclei (<1%)
           (MONIT-ERR) Monitor cross section (6%)
HISTORY    (20260702C) VT
ENDBIB              31
COMMON               2          3
ERR-1      MONIT-ERR
PER-CENT   PER-CENT
         4.         6.
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           38
